From: Pear contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: guard ARM64EC bitmap access for native ARM64 startup

Original Pear correction against Wine 4e819f054dd2d9ee855ee3f1e30d8c1bb8f80fcf.
The ARM64EC bitmap is allocated only for images with CHPE metadata. Test the
existing architecture/address guard before dereferencing that optional view,
so an unoptimized native ARM64 build does not access a null ARM64EC view while
initializing its first syscall context. Preserve the existing bitmap semantics.
Existing Wine LGPL-2.1-or-later notices apply.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -2792,15 +2792,16 @@
 
 /***********************************************************************
  *           is_emulated_code
  */
 BOOL is_emulated_code( ULONG_PTR ptr )
 {
-    const UINT64 *map = arm64ec_view->base;
+    const UINT64 *map;
     ULONG_PTR page = ptr / page_size;
     if (!is_arm64ec() || ptr >= (ULONG_PTR)user_space_limit) return FALSE;
+    map = arm64ec_view->base;
     return !((map[page / 64] >> (page & 63)) & 1);
 }
 
 
 /***********************************************************************
  *           alloc_arm64ec_map
